    <statement><p>The cost (in dollars) of producing <m>x</m>
air conditioners is <m>C = g(x) = 560 + 40 x</m>.
Find a formula for the inverse function
<m>g^{-1}(C)</m>.</p>
<p><m>g^{-1}(C) =</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{C-560}{40}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> SOLUTION </alert>




We solve the equation <m>C=g(x)=</m> for <m>x</m>. Subtract 560 from both
sides and divide both sides by 40 to get
<me>x=\frac{1}{40}(C-560).</me>
So
<me>g^{-1}(C)=\frac{1}{40}(C-560).</me>



</solution>
